        "descriptions": [
            {
                "value": "As a contribution to the 4th Workshop of the Measurement & Computation of Fire Phenomena (MaCFP) Working Group of the International Association for Fire Safety Science (IAFSS), the Institute of Building Materials, Concrete Construction and Fire Safety (iBMB) at Technische Universit\u00e4t Braunschweig generated a comprehensive experimental dataset. The dataset comprises results from thermogravimetric analysis (TGA), microscale combustion calorimetry (MCC) and cone calorimetry under both open and controlled atmosphere conditions. The key experimental parameters and experimental conditions are documented in the accompanying README file.",
                "descriptionType": "Abstract",
                "lang": "en"
            }
